  "reason": "The records collectively establish several relevant ingredients: ink-extrusion of powder–binder feedstocks followed by hydrogen treatment and sintering (R1, R9, R18), in-situ alloying from blended powders in refractory systems (R5, R8, R12), formation of dense single-BCC refractory HEAs by additive manufacturing (R7, R8, R11), and quench retention of a single BCC state in a closely related Nb–Ta–Ti–Zr-containing RHEA (R2). They therefore point toward printing a refractory HEA from mixed precursors and using thermal history to control its BCC phase. However, none discloses the decisive hydride-powder strategy for equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr, sequential decomposition governed by hydride formation enthalpies, deliberate oxygen uptake/gettering as an interstitial-strengthening tool, or a self-healing silicide coating. Reconstructing those specific coupled mechanisms would require a substantial new idea, so the set supports only partial reconstruction."
